<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan industrial output up 5.3 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan industrial output up 5.3 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in January increased a preliminary 5.3 percent from the previous month on a seasonally adjusted basis, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>MITI said in a statement that industrial output was on a gradual upward trend.  </p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>				  JAN	MONTH AGO     JAN INDEX</p>
<p> Output			 +5.3	+0.1	 105.5</p>
<p> Shipments		    +5.7	-0.2	 108.1</p>
<p> Inventories		   0.0	-0.4	 107.0</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 -3.8	-1.0	 107.5</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (pct):</p>
<p>				  JAN	MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			 +8.5	+3.7</p>
<p> Shipments		   +10.1	+4.3</p>
<p> Inventories		  -2.5	-1.9</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	-9.2	-4.4</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of MITI's forecasts for manufacturers' output:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted, month-on-month (in pct):</p>
<p>		     FEB forecast   MAR forecast</p>
<p>		     -3.3	     -2.7</p>
</text>
